1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,316
On Venus, a single day lasts longer than an entire year.

2
00:00:04,866 --> 00:00:08,379
Venus takes 225 Earth days to orbit the Sun.

3
00:00:08,779 --> 00:00:13,248
But it takes 243 Earth days to spin around just once.

4
00:00:13,748 --> 00:00:16,747
No planet in the solar system spins slower.

5
00:00:17,147 --> 00:00:18,620
And it spins backwards.

6
00:00:19,070 --> 00:00:22,781
So on Venus, the Sun rises in the west, and sets in the east.

7
00:00:23,231 --> 00:00:27,614
From one sunrise to the next takes about 117 Earth days.

8
00:00:28,014 --> 00:00:30,739
Just two sunrises in a whole Venus year.

9
00:00:31,189 --> 00:00:36,712
Under clouds of sulfuric acid, at around 465 °C.

10
00:00:37,262 --> 00:00:44,260
Could you survive a single day on Venus? And which planet should we explore next: Mars, or Mercury?
